|'''Bow of Faerdhinen:''' Your feedback has clearly shown that giving the Corrupted bow a 50% chance to save ammo charge rather than providing unlimited charges is not something you want.
|We've reverted this so that the Corrupted bow will once again provide unlimited charges, though for this additional convenience the number of shards required will be higher than that of the Blade of Saeldor (2,000 Crystal Shards rather than 1,000).

Q: Why does the Bow of Faerdhinen require 2,000 Crystal Shards to corrupt when the Blade of Saeldor only require 1,000?

A: We never specified in previous iterations of the blog exactly how many shards would be required to corrupt the bow.

Ranged weapons have a thematic feel about them where they typically require ammunition to use, which has an associated cost. Melee weapons don't typically follow that same trend (except for the Scythe of Vitur and the Wilderness weapons).

The initial feedback we received from many players suggested that having the Bow of Faerdhinen with no upkeep cost was too strong when compared to other Ranged items, so we opted for corruption to provide a 50% chance to save charges, rather than it provide an unlimited amount.

Your feedback has clearly shown this is not something you want, and as such we've reverted the corruption mechanic to once again provide unlimited charges, though for this additional convenience the price to corrupt the bow will be higher than that of the blade. This will help ensure that the bow remains balanced from a cost vs power perspective.
|}

