==Summary==
Now that we’ve been through all the changes let’s see how everything compares:

[[File:Equipment Rebalance- Ranged Meta Proposal (9).png|thumb|centre|600px|''Click the image for a larger version.'']]


The gaps have been filled, and there’s now a five weapon meta instead of a three weapon meta.

Here’s a reminder of the old meta:
* Twisted Bow against high Magic targets without low Defence
* Dragonhunter Crossbow against Dragons
* Toxic Blowpipe against everything else

And here’s what it’ll look like now:
* Twisted Bow against high Magic targets
* Dragonhunter Crossbow against Dragons
* Toxic Blowpipe against low Defence targets (up to around 20k effective Defence)
* Armadyl Crossbow against mid-high Defence targets when the boss has enough Hitpoints for Ruby Bolts to be effective
* Bow of Faerdhinen against mid-high Defence targets when Ruby Bolts would be ineffective

But that’s not all:
* Shields now substantially increase the DPS of 1-Handed Ranged weapons
* Crystal Armour has a defensive niche, as it provides better defence against Ranged attacks than Armadyl
* Crystal Armour is now usable with the Slayer Helmet
* A slight increase to Ranged strength on the Crystal Bow makes it more viable
* A small buff to Darts without the use of Toxic Blowpipe will increase their DPS
* A moderate buff to Chinchompas when using a Ranged offhand will increase their DPS

==Polling==
When this blog first released in May, we reiterated that most of the proposal here will be undertaken without a poll, due to being balancing and integrity changes. We also asked you how you felt about us polling some of the equipment stat buffs we’ve offered.

The feedback we received was mixed. Some players supported us polling as much as we were comfortable with, whilst others felt that players may naturally gravitate to voting for any positive changes offered.

We understand both perspectives, and we’ve made the choice to proceed with polling some of the changes. And ultimately we’ll use the voting trends here to inform how we might handle similar scenarios in the future.

